AB  - The objective of this study is to understand the temporal relationship between different brain waves and emotions using Electroencephalography (EEG) data. The temporal parameters such as mean, variance, standard-deviation, skewness and entropy has been extracted from the given database for emotion analysis using physiological signals (DEAP). Also, the Fast Fourier transform (FFT) has been used to analyze brain frequency bands from the time series EEG signals. The comparison between user emotion ratings and frequency bands has been done to confirm the EEG findings. To the collected data, the experimental results show how brain waves fluctuate with different types of emotions. These results can be helpful for Neurophysiological experts to collate the ground truth. Further, this will also help in assimilating the observations of different individuals with perspective of the brain activity due to the Mirror Neuron System (MNS). The promising performance of the statistical or temporal procedures with the EEG brain signals helps us to develop robust Human Interface Emotion Detection Systems which can be used for further research.
