AB  - A person with epilepsy, a brain disorder has at least two unprovoked seizures in a given time period. The recurring, spontaneous seizures that characterize epilepsy represent a chronic condition. In order to become clinically useful, an accurate description of seizures in a broad and heterogeneous population of patients must be overcome. In the proposed model, two screening approaches are deployed to diagnose epileptic seizures. Electro encephalogram (EEG) and Deep learning (DL) modalities. For feature extraction Convolution Neural Network (CNN) were implemented to discover the hidden pattern of the features. The signal changes are observed through time domain feature and frequency domain feature. In this study, Epileptic seizure dataset from Kaggle is downloaded. DL and modalities are examined for detecting automated epileptic seizures. The benefits and drawbacks of using DL-based approaches to diagnose epileptic seizures are discussed. A potential research avenue for automated epileptic seizure detection is discussed and the most promising DL models presented.
