AB  - Emotion recognition through EEG serves as a vital task within the realm of brain-computer interfaces (BCI). To improve recognition accuracy, this paper proposes an emotion recognition method based on 4D fusion features and coordinated attention mechanisms. First, the raw EEG signal undergoes a transformation, resulting in a 4D representation that encompasses frequency, space, and time, then a Convolutional Neural Network based on a Coordinated Attention (CACNN) mechanism is used to learn the frequency and spatial information in the 4D representation, and finally a long-time dependency in the 4D representation is extracted using a long short-term memory network (LSTM), and the classification results are output by the final layer of the LSTM. Our model achieves advanced performance on the single-subject DEAP dataset, with Arousal and Valence binary classification accuracies of 96.22 % and 95.75%.
