AB  - Emotion plays a vital role in human communication. Automatic understanding of human emotion by machines can improve human-machine interaction and be helpful for the diagnosis of mental disorders in psychiatric fields. Recent advancements in deep learning techniques help to classify human emotion using physiological signals like electroencephalogram (EEG). In this paper, a two-layer convolutional neural network is proposed to classify emotion from EEG signal. The network classifies the emotion using the correlation between different channels of the EEG signals recorded from the frontal region of the brain. The model is evaluated using DEAP dataset for valence and arousal dimension of the emotion. The subject independent training of the network with the EEG segments gives accuracy of 80.36% and 79.46%, F1 Score of 78.41 % and 75.52% for valence and arousal dimension respectively.
