AB  - Recently, emotional recognition based on machine learning algorithm has gained greater attention. Considering python has an excellent open-source model PyEEG which is especially made for dealing with EEG signal, and rich machine learning models, so we choose python as our tool. In this paper we have applied the analysis on DEAP: a database using physiological signal aiming for emotion analysis, which records arousal, valence, like/dislike levels, dominance and familiarity of 32 participants after watching 40 fragments of music videos. We use fast Fourier transform (FFT), “frequency ratio” and permutation entropy method to extract features from the dataset and divide the training set (80%) and the test set (20%), then build a three-dimensional convolution model(3D-CNN) to train them. Finally, we have achieved high precision (99.73%).
