AB  - Brain Monitoring through EEG offers a wide range of scope in assisting clinicians to monitor the brain's cognitive process for rehabilitation and therapeutic purposes. Such as monitoring the brain cognitive approach in fatigue (Coma, deep anesthesia, Exhausted) state in contrast with its ability in active state. There are many such wide areas in which users' cognitive ability can be monitored, nevertheless in all such areas EEG has offered new possibilities for brain computer interference in medical and non-medical purposes economically. In this paper we aim to classify the EEG signals recordings as active state signals or non- active state signals on raw data, rather than that of the using Feature Engineering, to explore new possibilities in cognitive recognition that Raw data offers. Although there was already much such research which uses Feature engineering as its core part in evaluating the EEG signals such as Time Frequency Domain features, or Entropy based measures, but we performed it on raw data by feeding the signal recordings to DEEP learning models. In the experiment conducted we aim to classify Raw EEG signals and perform comparative analysis on the deep neural network such as LSTM, LSTM with attention and BILSTM with highest accuracy received 98.5%. The results help us to conclude various results that is demonstrated in this paper.
