AB  - Epilepsy affects millions worldwide and requires accurate, timely detection for effective management. This study evaluates three deep learning models—Autoencoders (AE), Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN), and Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) to detect epileptic seizures using Electroencephalogram (EEG) data obtained from a publicly available dataset. The models were assessed by examining their accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score. The results of this study indicate that the Bi-directional LSTM outperformed the others, achieving a perfect accuracy of 100 %. This comparative analysis offers valuable insights for selecting optimal deep learning models in clinical applications, thereby supporting more effective diagnosing of epilepsy and improving patient outcomes.
